{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-ambient-space","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0245","math_ordinal":26,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"D is a subset of R^r and the asserted Minkowski sum C+D and proof both add vectors x+y; C must lie in the same r-dimensional ambient space.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt266.tex:69","source_normalized_sha256":"60f2525df72112cd960fada3bdfd2fafdedb653246bfa36eee6ec4ab757d4765","source_text":"$C\\subseteq\\Bbb R$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt266.tex:70","target_normalized_sha256":"1c931dc4e429819f2840e09427535e9ee6aadee7616cb85390a34228c985cb80","target_text":"$C\\subseteq\\Bbb R^r$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S266"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-coordinate-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0246","math_ordinal":85,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The vectors are defined with coordinates 1 through r and every following product and sum uses 1 through r; index 0 is undefined and adds a spurious factor.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt266.tex:180-181","source_normalized_sha256":"6a91af1a723d1cc46ded8a726cbd6276772397707fcffcc5dd3fae01cab9c4b8","source_text":"$\\prod_{i=0}^r(\\alpha'_i-\\alpha_i)^{1/r}+\\prod_{i=0}^r(\\beta'_i-\\beta_i)^{1/r}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt266.tex:182-183","target_normalized_sha256":"0b671e75fce0776b2f24d8346d3a0a059f5ae8a8f0e758c38fe16bc98cfb12ef","target_text":"$\\prod_{i=1}^r(\\alpha'_i-\\alpha_i)^{1/r}+\\prod_{i=1}^r(\\beta'_i-\\beta_i)^{1/r}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S266"}
{"classification":"mathematical-off-by-one-count","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0247","math_ordinal":108,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"A is presented as m+1 rectangles; when m=1 each nonempty side already contains one rectangle, so 'at most m-1' is impossible. The induction needs at most m rectangles, whose terminal index is at most m-1.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt266.tex:201","source_normalized_sha256":"a461b472cb41a9ec3dee5c90cf8e4a78252c9d82319adf75830031b8c309bfc6","source_text":"union of at most $m-1$ disjoint half-open intervals","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt266.tex:204","target_normalized_sha256":"62c66a7a5dd70c3146618063c344e531e6d4b59e379808443ce962b3abd63c5a","target_text":"gabungan paling banyak $m$ interval setengah terbuka yang saling lepas","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S266"}
{"classification":"mathematical-self-subtraction-typo","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0248","math_ordinal":116,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"B setminus B is empty, contradicting the immediately following nonempty split and every use of B-double-prime; it is the complement of the just-defined B-prime within B.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt266.tex:205","source_normalized_sha256":"d808ac596af96968dfef84db6b6ef2ce47e843d75ad265f46535a8eb64c58635","source_text":"$B''=B\\setminus B$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt266.tex:209","target_normalized_sha256":"bc23e72895597b584236715ab5093b010cc75e1438c7cb54089433cb0c6f7b03","target_text":"$B''=B\\setminus B'$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S266"}
{"classification":"mathematical-off-by-one-count","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0249","math_ordinal":119,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"B is presented as n+1 rectangles and a hyperplane cut can leave a piece of every rectangle on either side; when n=0 each nonempty piece is one rectangle, not zero. The induction still decreases through the A-side count.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt266.tex:206","source_normalized_sha256":"1b16b1df538ba12dc3f97edbb85caa7050d46c148134290feba80f8236c83db9","source_text":"unions of at most $n$ half-open intervals","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt266.tex:210","target_normalized_sha256":"1f97d653b7ed2d2be5caf6b568a7619bfdc112e35069f9a2b2be5ec4d71383cf","target_text":"gabungan paling banyak $n+1$ interval setengah terbuka","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S266"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-outer-measure-star","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0250","math_ordinal":179,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Part (f) treats arbitrary nonempty B, for which mu(B) need not be defined; translation invariance gives outer measure mu-star(x+B)=mu-star(B), exactly as in the theorem statement.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt266.tex:296","source_normalized_sha256":"4277f0128faf7205dee048b2a946be0d2b6723fbedae816f7334346091862b2d","source_text":"$(\\mu B)^{1/r}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt266.tex:302","target_normalized_sha256":"2964945e9a4b66d171e801f153d86de36576c7128ab65db2a89aaf447b8a5948","target_text":"$(\\mu^*B)^{1/r}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S266"}
